<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sena Gallica</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Senigallia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sena Gallica, modern Senigallia, is a town on the Adriatic coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marche">Marche</a>. It was the main centre of the Gallic Senones, who settled the area after sacking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> around 390 BCE. After defeating the Senones, Rome founded a colony there in the 280s BCE, one of its first on the Adriatic, and the region became the ager Gallicus.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sena-gallica.jpg" alt="Sena Gallica" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gaspa; MarkusMark; Luigi Chiesa; Steevie; derivative work by Number55 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Senigallia-collage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
